For the first success to occur on the third trial, the first two trials must be failures and the third trial must be a success.
The probability is
\[
\left(1-\frac{1}{4}\right)^2\cdot\frac{1}{4}
=\left(\frac{3}{4}\right)^2\cdot\frac{1}{4}
=\frac{9}{16}\cdot\frac{1}{4}
=\frac{9}{64}.
\]
Thus the required probability is \(\frac{9}{64}\).
